SageMaker real-time endpoints do not normally scale to zero, but cold-start-like behavior can be observed after:

Endpoint update
New deployment
Instance replacement
Scale-out event

Measure After Deployment

Immediately after endpoint reaches:

START=$(date +%s%3N)

aws sagemaker-runtime invoke-endpoint \
  --endpoint-name my-endpoint \
  --content-type application/json \
  --body fileb://request.json \
  response.json

END=$(date +%s%3N)

echo "Cold Start Latency: $((END-START)) ms"


